IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`
IMPORT `g7-art21-23-expressions`

-- g7-tests-fixtures-expressions: the fixtures of the tests of Articles 21 to 23 (entities, awareness, intent, statements and the 52 scenarios); no directive.
-- Tests of Articles 21 to 23 and their penalties.  Every expected set of contraventions was decided from the text of Articles 21, 22 and 23 (src:532-593) before this module was run:
--   21(1): not registered; said “registered by the Commissioner”; the entity itself, or another person the entity caused or permitted.   Strict.   Offence 21(10): fine of level 3.
--   21(2): not registered; said “registered”; the person knows, suspects or has reasonable grounds to suspect it is not; intends to mislead or to obtain property or a financial or OTHER advantage.  21(9): 2 years and a fine.
--   21(3): a Jersey entity, not registered; said “charity”; itself or caused/permitted.  Strict.   21(4): the same said by a person who is aware of BOTH that it is a Jersey entity and that it is not registered, and intends to mislead or to obtain
--          property or a financial advantage (not “other”).
--   21(5): not registered, not a Jersey entity, not an excepted foreign charity; said “charity” in connection with an activity in Jersey; itself or caused/permitted.   21(6): the person aware of BOTH, and intending as in 21(4).
--   23(1): an entity that does not meet all three conditions of 23(3) (registered, Jersey entity, managed or controlled in or from Jersey); said “Jersey charity”; itself or caused/permitted.   23(2): the knowing counterpart.
--   21(7), 23(5): (2), (4), (6) and 23(2) bind the person whether or not that person is the entity.   21(8), 23(4): a prescribed exception displaces the prohibitions.
-- The two alternative readings tested are the forks themselves: F7.4 (the knowing offence displaces the strict one) and F7.5 (“or other advantage” in (4), (6) and 23(2)).

§ `Part 6 — tests`

`fav` MEANS `the favoured interpretation`
`other F7.4` MEANS `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.4`
`other F7.5` MEANS `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.5`
`other F7.8` MEANS `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.8`
`other F7.12` MEANS `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.12`

§§ `Fixtures`

-- An entity, by whether it is a Jersey entity.  An entity falls within at least one sub-paragraph of Article 2(1) (domain.l4: `kinds of entity` is "empty if it is not an entity"): a Jersey entity here is a company,
-- a foreign one an entity substantially similar to one of the kinds, established under the law of another jurisdiction.  Its standing on the register is a separate input (`the entity is a registered charity`).
GIVEN jersey IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Entity
`an entity that is a Jersey entity` jersey MEANS
    Entity WITH name IS "An entity"
              , `standing on the register` IS `not on the register`
              , `kinds of entity` IS (IF jersey THEN LIST `a company` ELSE LIST `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction`)
              , `is a Jersey entity` IS jersey
              , governors IS EMPTY
              , purposes IS EMPTY

`a Jersey entity` MEANS `an entity that is a Jersey entity` TRUE
`a foreign entity` MEANS `an entity that is a Jersey entity` FALSE

-- A body that is NOT an entity: it falls within no sub-paragraph of Article 2(1) (a partnership; an NPO body corporate before paragraph (ba) was added on 16 October 2025).  The flag is the Jersey-entity flag
-- the caller supplies; a body that is not an entity should carry FALSE, and a TRUE flag on such a body is an inconsistent input that the Articles still do not reach.
GIVEN jersey IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Entity
`a body that falls within no sub-paragraph of Article 2(1), Jersey flag being` jersey MEANS
    Entity WITH name IS "A body that is not an entity"
              , `standing on the register` IS `not on the register`
              , `kinds of entity` IS EMPTY
              , `is a Jersey entity` IS jersey
              , governors IS EMPTY
              , purposes IS EMPTY

`a partnership that is not an entity` MEANS `a body that falls within no sub-paragraph of Article 2(1), Jersey flag being` FALSE
`an inconsistent body flagged as a Jersey entity but within no sub-paragraph of Article 2(1)` MEANS `a body that falls within no sub-paragraph of Article 2(1), Jersey flag being` TRUE

-- Awareness of one fact.
`no awareness` MEANS `Awareness of a fact under Articles 21 to 23` WITH knows IS FALSE, suspects IS FALSE, `reasonable grounds to suspect` IS FALSE
`knowledge` MEANS `Awareness of a fact under Articles 21 to 23` WITH knows IS TRUE, suspects IS FALSE, `reasonable grounds to suspect` IS FALSE
`suspicion` MEANS `Awareness of a fact under Articles 21 to 23` WITH knows IS FALSE, suspects IS TRUE, `reasonable grounds to suspect` IS FALSE
`reasonable grounds only` MEANS `Awareness of a fact under Articles 21 to 23` WITH knows IS FALSE, suspects IS FALSE, `reasonable grounds to suspect` IS TRUE

-- Awareness of the four facts, in this order: that the entity is not a registered charity; that it is a Jersey entity; that it is neither a Jersey entity nor an excepted foreign charity;
-- that it does not meet all of the conditions of Article 23(3).
GIVEN notRegistered IS AN `Awareness of a fact under Articles 21 to 23`
      jersey IS AN `Awareness of a fact under Articles 21 to 23`
      neither IS AN `Awareness of a fact under Articles 21 to 23`
      notAll IS AN `Awareness of a fact under Articles 21 to 23`
GIVETH AN `Awareness of the person making a statement`
`an awareness of` notRegistered jersey neither notAll MEANS
    `Awareness of the person making a statement` WITH
        `that the entity is not a registered charity` IS notRegistered
        `that the entity is a Jersey entity` IS jersey
        `that the entity is neither a Jersey entity nor an excepted foreign charity` IS neither
        `that the entity does not meet all of the conditions of Article 23(3)` IS notAll

-- Intent, in this order: to mislead as to the nature of the entity; to obtain property; to obtain a financial advantage; to obtain some other advantage.
GIVEN mislead IS A BOOLEAN
      property IS A BOOLEAN
      financial IS A BOOLEAN
      other IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Intent of the person making a statement`
`an intent of` mislead property financial other MEANS
    `Intent of the person making a statement` WITH
        `to cause another person to be misled as to the nature of the entity` IS mislead
        `to cause another person to give the entity any property` IS property
        `to cause another person to give the entity a financial advantage` IS financial
        `to cause another person to give the entity some other advantage` IS other

-- A statement, by what is said, whether it is in connection with an activity in Jersey, whether the entity makes it itself, whether the entity caused or permitted another person to make it, whether a
-- prescribed exception under Article 21(8) applies, whether one under Article 23(4) applies, and the awareness and the intent of the person making it.
GIVEN said IS A `What is said of an entity`
      inJersey IS A BOOLEAN
      itself IS A BOOLEAN
      caused IS A BOOLEAN
      exception21 IS A BOOLEAN
      exception23 IS A BOOLEAN
      awareness IS AN `Awareness of the person making a statement`
      intent IS AN `Intent of the person making a statement`
GIVETH A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23`
`a statement` said inJersey itself caused exception21 exception23 awareness intent MEANS
    `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` WITH
        `what is said of the entity` IS said
        `in connection with an activity of the entity in Jersey` IS inJersey
        `made by the entity itself` IS itself
        `the entity caused or permitted another person to make it` IS caused
        `an exception prescribed under Article 21(8) applies` IS exception21
        `an exception prescribed under Article 23(4) applies` IS exception23
        awareness IS awareness
        intent IS intent

